.\" Man page for cbzmanager — CBZ comic archive manager (GUI + headless CLI).
.\"
.\" Keep in sync with src/uclimode.pas (the CLI surface), README.md and
.\" the output of `cbzmanager --help`.
.TH CBZMANAGER 1 "August 2026" "cbzmanager 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cbzmanager \- CBZ comic archive manager (desktop application and headless CLI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cbzmanager
.RI [ command
.RI [ options ]]
.br
.B cbzmanager
.B validate
.I dir
.RB [ \-\-delete ]
.br
.B cbzmanager
.B convert\-webp
.I dir
.RB [ \-\-delete ]
.br
.B cbzmanager
.B merge
.I dir
.RB [ \-\-delete ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-\-chapters
.IR N1 , N2 , ...
.RB ]
.RB [ \-\-chapters\-per\-volume
.I N
.RB ]
.br
.B cbzmanager
.B \-\-help
.br
.B cbzmanager
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cbzmanager
is a Free Pascal / Lazarus desktop application for managing CBZ (Comic Book
ZIP) archives: validating archives, converting pages to WebP, merging
chapter files into volumes, editing pages in place, and handling
ComicInfo.xml metadata.
.PP
Launched without arguments, the desktop application starts (it requires a
graphical session).
.PP
When the first argument is a known command
.RB ( validate ,
.BR convert\-webp ,
.BR merge ,
.BR \-\-help ,
.BR \-\-version ),
the program runs
.I headless
as a command-line tool: no display server is needed, results are printed to
standard output, and the process exits with one of the exit statuses
described below.  Unknown or missing arguments fall through to the desktop
application.
.PP
Flags may appear before or after the directory argument.  The commands and
their semantics mirror the Python reference CLI
.RB ( cbz\-manager ,
in the
.I porting/cbz_manager
directory of the source tree); the operations
.BR delete\-pages ,
.BR find\-similar ,
and
.BR delete\-pages\-by\-id
are not ported.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B validate
.I dir
Verifies every
.I .cbz
file in
.I dir
with a deep check: the archive must be a valid ZIP and every image entry
must decode.  Prints one
.B OK
or
.B FAIL
line per file plus a summary.  Exits 0 when all files are valid, 1 when at
least one file fails.  The
.B \-\-delete
flag is accepted for compatibility with the reference CLI but has no
effect.
.TP
.B convert\-webp
.I dir
.RB [ \-\-delete ]
Converts the images of every
.I .cbz
file in
.I dir
to WebP at quality 75, keeping the WebP version only when it is smaller
than the original.  Existing WebP pages are left untouched,
ComicInfo.xml is stripped, and pages are renamed sequentially as
.IR page_NNNN.* .
The original file is renamed to
.I *_OLD.cbz
unless
.B \-\-delete
is given, in which case it is replaced in place.  Per-file failures are
reported and skipped; the exit status is always 0.
.TP
.B merge
.I dir
.RB [ options ]
Merges chapter files named
.RI "Series \- NNNN.cbz"
(or
.RI "Series \- SP01.cbz"
for specials) into volume files named
.RI "Series VNNN.cbz".
Every series found in
.I dir
is processed in turn.  Chapters-per-volume is auto-calculated from the
existing volumes as
.RI ( lowest_chapter \- 1) / num_volumes
(real division), falling back to 7 when no volumes exist or the value
would be below 1; see
.B \-\-chapters\-per\-volume
to override.  Only full volumes are created: chapters that do not fill a
complete volume are reported and skipped unless
.B \-\-force
is given.  Volume numbering continues after the highest existing volume.
Exits 0 on success or on a benign no-op ("not enough chapters", "no
chapter files"), 1 on error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-delete
Delete the original files after processing instead of renaming them to
.I *_OLD.cbz.
Valid for
.BR convert\-webp
and
.BR merge ;
accepted but unused for
.BR validate .
.TP
.B \-\-force
.B merge
only: append the remaining chapters to the last volume instead of
skipping them.  When there are fewer chapters than one full volume, a
single volume containing everything is produced.
.TP
.BI \-\-chapters " N1,N2,..."
.B merge
only: exact chapter counts per volume, comma-separated (for example
.BR "5,6,3" ).
A batch that does not fully fit the remaining chapters is skipped and its
chapters are left untouched.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-chapters\-per\-volume ;
using both is an error (exit status 1).
.TP
.BI \-\-chapters\-per\-volume " N"
.B merge
only: fixed number of chapters per volume.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-chapters .
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h ", " help
Print usage information and exit 0.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the program version and exit 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or a benign no-op (no chapter files found, not enough chapters,
no conversion savings).
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error: invalid directory, a failed operation, or
.B \-\-chapters
combined with
.BR \-\-chapters\-per\-volume .
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: missing directory, unknown option, or a malformed option
value.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I cbzmanager.log
Startup log written next to the executable.  Records, among other things,
which libwebp library was loaded (WebP support is optional and loaded
dynamically at runtime).
.SH EXAMPLES
Merge every series in a folder into volumes:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cbzmanager merge ~/manga/one-piece
.RE
.fi
.PP
Merge with a fixed 5 chapters per volume, absorbing leftovers into the
last volume:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cbzmanager merge --force --chapters-per-volume 5 ~/manga/one-piece
.RE
.fi
.PP
Convert a folder to WebP, deleting the originals:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cbzmanager convert-webp --delete ~/manga/archive
.RE
.fi
.PP
Deep-validate a folder of downloaded archives:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cbzmanager validate ~/manga/downloads
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The Python reference CLI
.B cbz\-manager
in the
.I porting/cbz_manager
directory of the source tree, and the project
.B README.md
(which documents the merge divergences from the reference implementation).
